 84	    /// storage independently. Within Ghostty, only `RenderState` reads
 85	    /// it, to know when to position its placements again. A renderer
 86	    /// should watch `RenderState.imagePlacementsGeneration` instead. For
 87	    /// example, a consumer of the storage would do:
 88	    ///
 89	    ///     if (storage.dirty != self.last_dirty) {
 90	    ///         self.last_dirty = storage.dirty;
 91	    ///         self.rebuildPlacements(storage);
 92	    ///     }
 93	    ///
 94	    /// Only compare values for equality. The counter wraps around on
 95	    /// overflow, so "greater than" has no meaning.
